    "result_text": "All 280 tests pass. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` flag on owner creation. When an owner is created, the response's `sharesHousehold` field is `true` if another owner already had the same address and city, otherwise `false` \u2014 creation still succeeds either way.\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **New function** `AssignOwnerSharesHousehold.java` \u2014 checks existing owners (before the new one is saved, so it never matches itself) for a matching address+city (case-insensitive) and sets the flag.\n\n2. **Pipeline wiring** `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `assignSharesHousehold` step (under the `transaction` governance) between `assignNamesakeCount` and `save`.\n\n3. **Domain model** `Owner.java` \u2014 added a persisted `sharesHousehold` (`Boolean`, `shares_household` column) with getter/setter, following the `namesakeCount` pattern. Persisting it is required because the test reads the value back via a fresh `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n4. **Schemas** \u2014 added the `shares_household BOOLEAN` column to the hsqldb, h2, postgres, and mysql `owners` tables.\n\n5. **API contract** `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `sharesHousehold` boolean to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto`; MapStruct maps it automatically by name.\n\nThe new `Cp17Tests` passes and the full suite (280 tests) is green.",
